slimserve: glm53f-q2-1 is not ready on Apple Silicon (Metal): single-stream serving is qualified, concurrent serving is not: batching buys almost nothing on this record. Every exact-token gate on this profile is concurrency 1, and they all pass bit-identically (8tok 7dd30ea193a6, off1-2000 393882a2ddaf, 2500x64 1d7d58486dc7) at 34-40 tok/s decode and 237-258 t/s prefill, beating ds4 on the same box by ~1.5x and ~1.8x. Concurrent serving runs but does not scale: the GPU step time grows linearly with the number of rows in flight, so six concurrent requests aggregate 41.2 tok/s against 40.0 for one. The record stays gated until concurrent exact-token gates exist and batching earns its keep; the plan is the batching campaign section of HANDOFF.md. SLIMSERVE_SERVE_IN_PROGRESS=1 boots it meanwhile. Continuing: SLIMSERVE_SERVE_IN_PROGRESS=1.
